    "evidence_text": "Therefore, the model trained with the proposed training framework reduces relative 14\\% character error rate, compared to original model which has the similar real-time capability.\n\nEMA method is utilized with model averaging and BMUF to further decrease the character error rate (CER).\n\nHowever, it also leads to much more computation and higher RTF, so that the recognition result can not be displayed in real time.\n\na softmax layer with 11088 hidden markov model (HMM) tied-states as output classes, the loss function is cross-entropy (CE).\n\nThe performance metric of the system in Mandarin is reported with character error rate (CER).\n\nThe Shenma test set including about 9000 samples and Amap test set including about 7000 samples contain various real world conditions.\n\nSecondly, for real world applications, very deep LSTM is distilled to a shallow one, so as for lower RTF.\n\nA comparison between 6-layers and 9-layers sMBR models shows that 3 additional layers of layer-wise training brings relative 12.6% decreasing of CER.\n\nlayers decreases absolute 0.73% approximately compared with CE models, so the improvement of sequence discriminative learning is promising.",
